MODIFICATIONS MADE BY THE AUTHORS OF THIS WORK
----------------------------------------------
Added (this paper's contribution):
  * The PER protocol environment and rules
    (agentverse/environments/tasksolving_env/per.py and rules/per.py,
     rules/evaluator/per.py).
  * The broadcast-deliberation protocol with confidence polling and an approval
    phase (environments/tasksolving_env/broadcast_deliberation.py and its rule).
  * The single-agent-reflect and single-LLM-benchmark environments used as the
    matched baselines.
  * The deliberator agent, the failure-memory rule, and the Omni-MATH output
    parsers (mgsm, mgsm-evaluator, mgsm-critic-route, mgsm-critic-agree).
  * The entire trace-metrics layer: agentverse/metrics/** and the RQ analysis
    entry points in agentverse_command/ that compute the paper's process metrics
    (reviewer precision, CouplingRate, ReviewerGuidedRepairRate, the inner-loop
    transition decomposition, and the strict-coupling audit).
  * The evaluator contract in agentverse/evaluation/**.
  * The benchmark harness agentverse_command/benchmark.py and config resolution.
  * The 2x5 symmetric-transition pipeline in src/precise_uncoupled/process/.

Changed relative to upstream AgentVerse:
  * The OpenAI client (agentverse/llms/openai.py) was extended with retry,
    rate-limit backoff and per-example token accounting.
  * Per-example resource accounting was fixed so counters reset between
    problems (see docs/LIMITATIONS.md -- the legacy pre-fix values are withdrawn).

Changed FOR THIS RELEASE specifically (not present in the research repository):
  * Author-private absolute default paths were replaced with repository-relative,
    environment-overridable ones.
  * Facility-specific endpoint workarounds were made generic and opt-in; no
    endpoint URL, hostname, token or credential ships here.
  * Import-time side effects that wrote log files into the source tree were made
    opt-in.
  Every such edit is marked with a "RELEASE PATCH" comment in the source and is
  listed in docs/PROVENANCE.md.

Removed relative to upstream AgentVerse:
  * The simulation half of AgentVerse (simulation environments and agents, the
    Gradio GUI and demo, tool-using executors) and the BMTools integration. None
    is used by this paper; see docs/PROVENANCE.md for the complete list.

